WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.774
Vague promises do not sell.

00:00:01.774 --> 00:00:04.614
Specific promises invite a yes or a no.

00:00:04.614 --> 00:00:07.453
This lesson is about promise that is specific.

00:00:07.453 --> 00:00:08.872
Vague promises don't sell.

00:00:08.872 --> 00:00:11.357
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.357 --> 00:00:14.906
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.906 --> 00:00:20.229
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.229 --> 00:00:24.133
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:28.392
Stay practical: rewrite a vague promise before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.712 --> 00:00:31.658
Help you grow and unlock potential is fog.

00:00:31.658 --> 00:00:34.972
Name the outcome, the who, and a time box.

00:00:34.972 --> 00:00:37.549
Remember the objective: rewrite a vague promise.

00:00:37.549 --> 00:00:41.600
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.019
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:46.019 --> 00:00:50.069
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:50.069 --> 00:00:54.488
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:54.808 --> 00:00:59.102
Rewrite a vague promise into one sentence a stranger can test.

